course: dictionary
lesson: 1951
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. Look at the words around the word, because they leave clues. «Christians remember the Last Supper in Holy Communion.» Christians, Last Supper and Holy all point to church, so communion here is a church service.
explain: «The altar or communion table is where the bread and wine are prepared for communion.» Bread and wine are part of a service, so communion means the sharing of bread and wine in church. Check by swapping in your meaning and asking if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «She felt a deep communion with nature on the hill.» There is no church here, so the clue is a feeling. Communion can also mean a close sharing of thoughts or feelings. When you meet a word that could mean two things, look for the clue that picks the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Holy Communion is a Christian service in which people share bread and wine (or juice) to remember Jesus and his Last Supper.
fact: Holy Communion is also called the Eucharist, the Mass or the Lord's Supper.
fact: «First Communion» is the special day when a Catholic child first receives communion, often with family celebrating.
fact: Communion can also mean a close sharing of thoughts or feelings, as in «in communion with nature».
exercise: «Christians remember the Last Supper in Holy Communion.» What is Holy Communion? | A type of bread baked at Easter | *A church service where people share bread and wine (or juice) | A school trip to the seaside | A kind of music played on drums
exercise: «She felt a deep communion with nature on the hill.» What does communion mean here? | A type of rock | A loud argument | *A close sharing of thoughts or feelings | A meal eaten outdoors
exercise: «Maya's First Communion was a special day for her family.» What is First Communion? | A visit to the doctor | A birthday party for a grown-up | *A day when a Catholic child first receives communion | The first day of school
test: «The altar or communion table is where the bread and wine are prepared for communion.» What are the bread and wine prepared for? | Feeding the birds | Packing a picnic | Baking a cake for a party | *The service of communion
test: Which is another name for Holy Communion? | *The Eucharist | Lunch in the school hall | Bedtime | The Easter Bunny
exam: Which words in «Christians remember the Last Supper in Holy Communion» are the clues that communion is a church word? | The and in | Holy and in | Remember and the | *Christians and Last Supper
